\ events.fam — the node's events (docs/TIMING_FIXES.md, section 2 and
\ item 15), after headers.fam and before pool.fam: what happens, numbered
\ from 1, the last EVN kept in a ring for GET /v1/events?after=<n>
\ (api.fam), so a wallet waits for them rather than asking again.
\
\ An event is EVSZ bytes: +0 its number, +4 its kind, +8 a height, +C a
\ state (the kind's), +10 an id (32 bytes), +30 another (32 bytes).
\ - EVBLK, a block connected: its height and id (sync.fam's nconnect).
\ - EVUNDO, a block undone: its height and id (nundo).
\ - EVTX, a transaction: its id and its state (pool.fam): EVPOOLED;
\   EVREPL replaced (+30: by which); EVEVICT evicted for one paying more;
\   EVMINED mined (the height: its first output in that block); EVCONF
\   out of the pool otherwise (an input spent by another, an operation
\   failing now); EVBACK back in the pool after blocks were undone.
\ - EVSTAT, the node's state when it changes (api.fam's aevst): ESYNCED,
\   ESYNCING (behind its best header by more than a block), ENOPEERS;
\   the height, and +10 the best header's height.
\
\ evput ( kind height state id other -- )  an event (id and other: 32
\ bytes each, or 0 for zeros); the ring made at the first.
\ evat ( n -- a )  where event n is, if still kept (evlow to evn @).
\ evlow ( -- n )  the oldest number kept (1 before the ring has wrapped).
\ evn ( -- addr )  the newest event's number, and evh the lock an event
\ is written under: two cells of their own (evmk, with the ring), not
\ variables, so that a thread with variables of its own (the API's,
\ api.fam: made after them) reads the same count, and copies events out
\ under the lock, none half written or being written over.

:M EVN 800 lit ;
:M EVSZ 50 lit ;
:M EVBLK 1 lit ;  :M EVUNDO 2 lit ;  :M EVTX 3 lit ;  :M EVSTAT 4 lit ;
:M EVPOOLED 1 lit ;  :M EVREPL 2 lit ;  :M EVEVICT 3 lit ;  :M EVMINED 4 lit ;  :M EVCONF 5 lit ;  :M EVBACK 6 lit ;
:M ESYNCED 1 lit ;  :M ESYNCING 2 lit ;  :M ENOPEERS 3 lit ;

: evr variable ;  : evh variable ;  : eva variable ;  : evk variable ;
: evmk  evh @ 0= if 8 lit alloc dup evh !  2 lit wzero  EVN EVSZ * malloc evr ! then ;
: evn  evmk  evh @ 4 lit + ;
: evat  EVN 1 lit - and EVSZ * evr @ + ;
: evlow  evn @ EVN u< if 1 lit else evn @ EVN - 1 lit + then ;
\ evid ( src dst -- )  32 bytes, or zeros for src 0.
: evid  swap ?dup if swap 20 lit bcopy else 8 lit wzero then ;
: evput
evmk
evr @ 0= if 2drop 2drop drop else
	evh @ lock
	evn @ 1 lit + dup evk !  evat eva !
	eva @ 30 lit + evid  eva @ 10 lit + evid
	eva @ C lit + !  eva @ 8 lit + !  eva @ 4 lit + !  evk @ eva @ !
	\ its number last: an event counted is one written whole
	evk @ evn !
	evh @ unlock
then ;
